# True Graph Refactor Implementation Plan

## Goal

Replace the hand-wired mux2 shim with a proper GraphExecutor-based implementation where:
- All events (input AND force feedback) flow through the graph
- MuxNode routes FF to the active source based on mode
- Single event loop driven by GraphExecutor

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Event Flow"
        GS1[SourceNode<br>Primary] -->|CtrlEvent::Input| MUX[MuxNode]
        GS2[SourceNode<br>Assist] -->|CtrlEvent::Input| MUX
        MUX -->|CtrlEvent::Input| SINK[SinkNode]
        SINK -->|CtrlEvent::FF| MUX
        MUX -->|CtrlEvent::FF| GS1
        MUX -->|CtrlEvent::FF| GS2
    end
```

Key insight: **FF events flow backwards through the same graph**. MuxNode receives FF from SinkNode and routes to the appropriate physical source based on mode state.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Core Node Implementations

#### [NEW] `src/core/nodes/source.rs` - GilrsSourceNode

A node that wraps gilrs and emits CtrlEvents. Also receives FF events and forwards them to the physical device.

```rust
pub struct SourceNode {
    driver: GilrsDriver,          // polls gilrs events
    ff_dev: Option<PhysicalFFDev>, // for FF forwarding
    gamepad_id: GamepadId,
}

impl Node for SourceNode {
    fn process(&mut self, port: PortId, event: CtrlEvent, ctx: &mut ProcessContext) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
        match event {
            CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff) => {
                // Forward FF to physical device
                self.handle_ff(ff);
                vec![]
            }
            _ => vec![] // Source doesn't process input events inbound
        }
    }
    
    fn tick(&mut self) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
        // Poll gilrs and emit events on output port
        self.poll_events()
    }
}
```

---

#### [NEW] `src/core/nodes/sink.rs` - EvdevSinkNode

A node that receives CtrlEvents and writes them to a virtual device. Also reads FF events from the virtual device and emits them as CtrlEvents.

```rust
pub struct SinkNode {
    device: VirtualDevice,
}

impl Node for SinkNode {
    fn process(&mut self, port: PortId, event: CtrlEvent, ctx: &mut ProcessContext) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
        match event {
            CtrlEvent::Input(input) => {
                self.write_input(input);
                vec![]
            }
            _ => vec![]
        }
    }
    
    fn tick(&mut self) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
        // Read FF events from virtual device and emit as CtrlEvents
        self.poll_ff_events()
    }
}
```

---

#### [MODIFY] [src/core/nodes/mux.rs](file:///home/ruffsl/git/ruffsl/CtrlAssist/src/core/nodes/mux.rs) - Update MuxNode for Bidirectional FF

Add handling for FF events - route them to the appropriate source based on mode:

```rust
fn process(&mut self, port: PortId, event: CtrlEvent, ctx: &mut ProcessContext) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
    match event {
        CtrlEvent::Input(input) => {
            // Existing input processing logic
            self.process_input(port, input, ctx)
        }
        CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff) => {
            // Route FF based on mode
            self.route_ff(ff)
        }
        _ => vec![]
    }
}

fn route_ff(&self, ff: FFEvent) -> Vec<(PortId, CtrlEvent)> {
    match self.mode {
        MuxModeType::Priority => {
            // FF to both (or could be configurable)
            vec![
                (ports::MUX_PRIMARY_IN, CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff.clone())),
                (ports::MUX_ASSIST_IN, CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff)),
            ]
        }
        MuxModeType::Toggle => {
            // FF only to active controller
            vec![(self.toggle_active_port, CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff))]
        }
        MuxModeType::Average => {
            // FF to both
            vec![
                (ports::MUX_PRIMARY_IN, CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff.clone())),
                (ports::MUX_ASSIST_IN, CtrlEvent::ForceFeedback(ff)),
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

